## Existing code: gate only new violations

This harness was rendered for existing code (`swift_adoption: existing`), so the
gate doesn't fail on code nobody touched. Record the decision and its numbers in
`docs/decisions/0001-gate-new-format-and-lint-only.md`.

- Set `.swift-format` to the code's existing style (indentation, line length)
  first; don't reformat the codebase to match the template's default.
- swift-format checks only Swift files changed since the merge-base with `main`
  (`HEAD~1` when on `main`; `HARNESS_BASE_REF` overrides). CI fetches full history.
- SwiftLint checks every file against `.harness/swiftlint-baseline.json`. The owner
  writes it once with `scripts/swift-quality.sh write-baseline` and commits it.
  Never regenerate it to make a change pass; shrink it as old violations go.
- The first edit to an old file reformats that whole file through the hook.
- When adopting, keep the project's own Package.swift and build scripts: render
  with `--skip` for files that exist and `--exclude Sources --exclude Tests
  --exclude Package.swift` to leave out the sample package.
